      "content": "Even if the drops are only a few months old, using them without knowing the exact contamination risk from the cleaner is risky. You should not put any medication in your eye if the chemical exposure is still an active issue. If the irritation is mild, keep rinsing with clean water, but if it persists, you must call your primary care doctor or an urgent care clinic for professional advice.",
